# Attribute definitions (Elementplan)

Write attribute `definition` fields under `attributes[].definition`.

## Templates by type

### Simple (Name, Reference, Elevation)

One sentence; plain language.

### Enum / allowed_values

```yaml
definition:
  de: |-
    {What this attribute means}

    **Zulässige Werte**
    - `TOKEN` — translated label   # opaque code (IFC enum, BKP, …)
    - `KlartextToken`              # already plain language in this locale – no gloss
```

Headers: Zulässige Werte (de) / Valeurs admises (fr) / Valori ammessi (it) / Allowed values (en).
Gloss after the em dash only when the token is an opaque code; never when the
token is already plain language in that language (see Rules).

### Schema-backed value lists (room-name, product-class, …)

Meaning only in the attribute. Provenance and version live on `values/<slug>.yaml`
(`norm_reference`, description URL). Pinning is done by pointing `allowed_values`
at a versioned catalogue ID (e.g. `…-v0.2.0`), not by writing version numbers in
prose.

**IFC stores the classification label (`prefLabel` / name), never the notation
(code).** Codes stay in the published schema and in book appendix rows for
bridging (BKP/KBOB). `values/*.yaml` and attribute prose use the name that goes
into the model – same pattern as room names (`Schlafzimmer`, not `RN-…`).

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — notation in IFC / prose examples
Blattnotation (z. B. `AOF-03-01`) … Elternklasse (`AOF-01` bis `AOF-04`)

# ✅ GOOD — name in IFC / prose examples
Blattbezeichnung (z. B. `Kies`) bei bekanntem Belag; sonst die Elternklasse
(z. B. `Versiegelt`, `Teildurchlässig`, `Durchlässig`, …)
```

Link the catalogue name to the schema page URL taken from that value file’s
`description` (same URL in all four languages):

```yaml
definition:
  de: |-
    {What this attribute means}

    **Zulässige Werte**
    - Siehe Werteliste [{catalogue name}](https://schema.pragmaticbim.ch/classification/{page}.html).
allowed_values: pragmaticbim:value/{slug}
```

Do **not** put bare `schema.pragmaticbim.ch` URLs, `v0.2.0`, “latest”, or
“continuously published” wording in attribute prose – only the markdown link on
the catalogue name. The book converter prints the URL address after the name
so print PDFs stay usable without clicking.
### IFC2x3 substitute

Same as enum, plus:

```yaml
    **Hinweis**
    - IFC2x3-Ersatz für {IFC4+ attribute name in plain language}.
```

### Fixed boolean (allowed_values)

State expected value in plain language; optional **Zulässige Werte** for `TRUE` / `FALSE`.

### Quantity (Qto_* psets)

Describe what is measured and the unit only. **Never** mention abstractBIM, workflows, or downstream tools.

### Calculated / derived (e.g. CalculatedType)

Short meaning + logic name + example. **Do not** put FEEL, Entscheidungstabelle, or book Anhang pointers on the attribute – those live in book Anhang D, Bauteiltypisierung. Attribute text must also work in the webapp, which has no Anhang.

```yaml
definition:
  de: |-
    Berechneter Typname für Kosten- und Mengengruppierung. Logik `{LogicName}`.
    Beispiel: `{ExampleToken}`
```

For shared logics with a fixed prefix per element (e.g. `PlattenTypisierung`):

```yaml
    Berechneter Typname für Kosten- und Mengengruppierung. Logik `PlattenTypisierung` (Prefix `Decke`).
    Beispiel: `Decke_Beton_250mm_REI90_53`
```

Headers/labels: Beispiel (de) / Exemple (fr) / Esempio (it) / Example (en).

## Rules

1. Lead with plain-language meaning, not datatype.
2. IFC enum tokens stay exact in backticks; translate the label after em dash
   (`` `NEW` — Neubau ``). The gloss is for opaque codes, not for tokens that are
   already plain language in that locale.
3. **No tautological gloss.** When the token is already German (or already FR/IT/EN
   in that language block) and self-explanatory, list the token alone – do not
   repeat or lightly paraphrase it after the em dash.

   ```yaml
   # ❌ BAD — token is already German
   - `Intern` — intern
   - `Hochgesichert` — hochgesichert
   - `Öffentlich` — öffentlich zugänglich

   # ✅ GOOD — opaque IFC/code token needs a gloss
   - `NEW` — Neubau
   - `USERDEFINED` — benutzerdefiniert

   # ✅ GOOD — localized plain-language token, no gloss
   - `Öffentlich`
   - `Intern`
   - `Eingeschränkt`
   - `Hochgesichert`
   ```

   Same in FR/IT/EN: `` `Interne` — interne `` and `` `Restricted` — restricted ``
   are wrong; list the token alone. Only add a gloss when it adds meaning the
   token does not already carry (e.g. `` `GAB` — Grundausbau … ``).
4. Do not translate tokens in `values/*.yaml` arrays.
5. Quantity attributes: geometry/measurement only – no vendor or workflow references.
6. All four languages: same structure; translate labels, not enum tokens.
7. **Write from German, not from English word order.** FR/IT must sound native; do not calque EN.
8. Schema version / provenance live on the value catalogue. In attribute text, only a
   markdown link on the catalogue name is allowed (URL copied from that catalogue).
9. **Schema-backed classifications: name in IFC, not code.** Opaque IFC enums and
   project codes (BKP, eBKP-H) stay as codes; SKOS notations with a separate
   human label do not.

## Tone / calques (do not use)

| Concept | de | fr (native) | it (native) | avoid |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Marks whether | Kennzeichnet | Indique si | Indica se | FR *Identifie si*, IT *Identifica se* |
| MEP medium | Medium | fluide | fluido | FR *médium*, IT *mezzo* |
| derive / derivable | ableitbar | déductible / peut être déduit | ricavabile | FR *dérivable*, IT *derivabile* from EN |
| below terrain | unter Terrain | sous le niveau du terrain | sotto il livello del terreno | FR *sous terrain* |
| cost bearer | Kostenträger | imputation | imputazione | FR *support de coûts* |
| fire R (Tragfähigkeit) | Tragfähigkeit | stabilité | capacità portante | FR *portance* |
| tenant placeholder | `{Mietername}` | `{nom du locataire}` | `{nome locatario}` | German token in FR/IT |

Do not translate IFC/property tokens or enum tokens in backticks.
